 ('Nikhil','nikhil.lnu@sdstate.edu',16,'Nikhil’s research focuses on the soil microbiome and its practical applications, particularly the discovery of beneficial microbial strains with biostimulant and disease-suppressive potential. His work aims to translate these discoveries into new microbial products for farmers.'),
 ('Israel Akinlabi','israel.akinlabi@sdstate.edu',17,'Israel’s research focuses on the evolution of NLR immune receptors, particularly how they acquire additional integrated domains (NLR-IDs). His work examines how these domains contribute to pathogen recognition, specificity, and immune response in the Rpg5 NLR-ID-mediated immune system in barley.'),
 ('Mrinmoy Sarker','Mrinmoy.Sarker@sdstate.edu','mrinmoy-sarker','Mrinmoy’s research focuses on identifying temperature-sensitive motifs in cereal immune receptors and understanding their role in plant defense. His work particularly examines the RMRL-mediated immune system in barley and wheat and how temperature influences innate immune responses.'),
